00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:21.029
One of the most interesting things about the
Saw franchise is that nobody is ever portrayed

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:24.430
without major flaws, even among the so called
good guys.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:28.560
There is perhaps no better example of this
than the father and son pair: Eric and Daniel

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.560
Matthews.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.950
Welcome to Horror History, my name is Deathbelle
Delphine and I will be your instructor today

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.700
as we cover Eric and Daniel Matthews.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.000
This father and son first appeared in Saw
II, but their story stretches back much further

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.000
than that.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.080
So let’s take it back.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.050
Eric Matthews was born in the late 60s or
early 70s.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:51.010
He would become a homicide detective for the
Metropolitan Police Department known for his

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.140
uncompromising attitude, where he was well
respected earlier in his career, but his crumbling

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.260
home life eventually seeped into his job.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.470
He had trouble in his marriage sometime after
he and his wife gave birth to their son,

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.520
Daniel, in the early 90s.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.330
Though the first cause of his marital troubles
are not known, it was likely that Eric’s

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.330
infidelity was the final straw before his
wife filed for divorce.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.430
In 2000, these home issues had begun to manifest
themselves in his work life.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.240
The first known incident happened when he
broke a suspect’s jaw with his flashlight.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.050
He has also been criticized for gunning down
an unarmed suspect and planting evidence on

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.250
criminals in order to get an easier conviction.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:27.800
It was around 2003 when Eric had an affair
with his female partner, Allison Kerry.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.060
Not only did he lose his marriage because
of this, but he also stopped working with

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.250
Ms. Kerry and lost custody of his son, who
was entering his teenage years.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.560
Daniel began acting out, and I think it was
because his father was a cop that he chose

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.550
a life of petty crime to get back at him.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.570
The seriousness of these crimes rode the line
of a punishable offense, so Daniel managed

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:45.800
to stay out of juvy.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.090
In 2005, while still in the process of getting
the divorce, the media caught wind of Eric’s

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.000
foul… wind.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:52.960
*laughter*

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.120
That sounds nasty.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.440
A KCUD 2 news crew confronted him one night
about rumors of police brutality, causing

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.580
Eric to snap.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.660
“... use brutality against suspects.”

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:02.580
“What brutality?

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.680
Let me tell you something!

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.900
What brutality?

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.920
What brutality?

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:06.420
Huh?

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.420
What brutality?

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:08.880
WHAT?

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:14.300
Where’s my cigarette?”

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.760
Not only was Matthews suspended for excessive
use of force and implicated in evidence tampering,

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.620
but the news footage appeared in a TV documentary,
and only worsened his already waning reputation.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.920
If we take a look at the meltdown meter, he
was basically at the level of Elle Mills.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.230
"This is all I ever wanted.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.100
And why the **** am I so ****ing unhappy?

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.010
This... it doesn't make any ****ing sense."

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.730
Eric never really got back into the field
after his suspension, instead opting to take

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:42.030
desk work and causing follow of his fellow
cops to question his dedication to the job.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:46.200
That would change, however, when the other
side of the law made things more personal.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.819
In October of 2005, Eric received a call that
his son had been caught shoplifting at a store

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:52.270
called Superior Electronics.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:55.800
He picks him up and is unable to get through
to him, they just end up arguing.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.780
It was Eric’s turn to be in charge of the
kid, but Daniel decides he’d like to go

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.270
back to his Mom’s house early, and he storms
off without saying goodbye.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.710
Daniel never makes hit back to his mother’s
house though, he is abducted by a man named

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:09.650
Obi, who is working for a criminal who is
just starting to pick up some notoriety in

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.690
the city, a man only known to the public as
Jigsaw.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:16.290
When Daniel wakes up, he finds himself in
a room with seven other criminals and notices

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.230
they are being recorded by a video camera.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.840
The last to wake up is a woman named Amanda,
who finds a key with a hidden tape recorder

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.959
that tells them they are breathing in a deadly
nerve gas that would kill them in two hours,

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:29.560
but the doors to the house would not open
until three hours had elapsed.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.670
They are tasked with finding the antidotes
hidden around the house.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.360
A couple clues are given.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.940
“One is inside the safe in front of you.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.360
You all possess the combination to the safe.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.540
Think hard.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.280
The numbers are in the back of your mind.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.820
The clue to their order can be found over
the rainbow.”

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.320
He also tells them to think about what they
have in common, and, as usual, X marks the

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.330
spot.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.090
“You are a pirate!”

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.520
So, in true pirate fashion, the first guy
to try to escape gets his face blown off,

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.030
leaving Daniel and the others to scavenge
the halls of the Nerve Gas House for more

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.900
clues, and before you type your comment telling
me to look for clues, yes, I am aware I look

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:09.900
like Shaggy.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:10.900
Get over it!

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.530
"I'm fixing me a super Shaggy sandwich!"

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:16.090
Now the reason Daniel is being tested is not
specifically stated.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:20.019
It could be for not appreciating his time
with his father, who really just has the kid’s

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:23.979
best interests in mind... but it’s probably
because he is veering off into a life of crime,

00:04:23.979 --> 00:04:27.370
because part of what they all have in common
is that they’ve committed crimes, even if

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.669
the ones Daniel committed are much less severe
than the others.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:33.009
Many of the victims who make it out of the
victims who come out of Jigsaw’s traps are

00:04:33.009 --> 00:04:36.490
rehabilitated, and begin to cherish their
lives after they recover.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:40.080
Daniel is probably one of the best examples
where you can see him changing in real time

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.229
as he watches the big guy, Xavier, trying
to smash down a door.

00:04:43.229 --> 00:04:45.629
You can see Daniel flinching with each and
every hit.

00:04:45.629 --> 00:04:49.360
With each strike Xavier pounds into the door,
he’s also pounding the picture of how scary

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.639
life in prison can be into the teenager’s
head.

00:04:51.639 --> 00:04:55.289
Another thing to note about this scene is
that Daniel is the calmest person out the

00:04:55.289 --> 00:04:58.870
group, and perhaps the reason he is able to
last longer in the Nerve Gas House than any

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.759
of the others is because he isn’t doing
as much heavy breathing.

00:05:01.759 --> 00:05:05.710
Also, Jigsaw doesn’t typically test kids,
though I would love to one of those spin-off

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.680
series’ where it would basically be called
Saw Babies or some ****.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:12.740
But despite perhaps being in less danger early
on in this game, the others would soon make

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:16.400
a discovery that made Daniel Matthews the
biggest target of all.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.360
Jigsaw, the evil mastermind of the Saw franchise,
managed to outsmart his opponents with his

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.360
razor sharp intellect.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:28.009
But what if the opposition had been a little
bit smarter?

