00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:33.220
After one of the women, Laura, finds a secret
basement, Daniel joins the group to investigate,

00:06:33.229 --> 00:06:37.180
and they find a mannequin with a note for
Obi, explaining the rules of his furnace trap,

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.699
where he was unsuccessful in obtaining 2 antidotes.

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:43.490
Laura starts getting woozy after this and
Daniel encourages her not to stop and rest.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:47.699
He offers her a sense of optimism which shows
Jigsaw that the way he behaves with his dad

00:06:47.699 --> 00:06:51.449
really is just a result of him lashing out
and he is genuinely a good kid.

00:06:51.449 --> 00:06:55.139
Daniel asks Amanda why she was chosen for
the game, and she tells of how she was a junkie

00:06:55.139 --> 00:06:59.419
who was once framed for possession, but Daniel
does not yet know that it was really his father

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.449
who put her behind bars.

00:07:00.449 --> 00:07:03.520
That’s gonna be an AWKWARD CONVERSATION
if it ever comes up.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.520
…

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:08.439
One of the other guys comes to let them know
they found an unlocked door, and Daniel displays

00:07:08.439 --> 00:07:12.339
his kind heart once again by helping the deteriorating
Laura down the stairs.

00:07:12.339 --> 00:07:16.819
The next game is for Xavier, but he selfishly
throws Amanda into the pit instead, which

00:07:16.819 --> 00:07:20.439
Daniel bravely helps her climb out of, even
in the shadow of Xavier’s deteriorating

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.439
sanity.

00:07:21.439 --> 00:07:24.659
As they search for the next room, the group
tries to figure out one of Jigsaw’s clues

00:07:24.659 --> 00:07:26.869
by determining what it is that they all have
in common.

00:07:26.869 --> 00:07:30.969
The only shared thread seems to be that all
of them have been to jail… of of them, except

00:07:30.969 --> 00:07:31.969
Daniel.

00:07:31.969 --> 00:07:33.009
But as it turns out...

00:07:33.009 --> 00:07:35.360
Daniel is the very reason that each of them
are linked.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.040
The reason is unveiled when Laura finds the
X.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.360
X marks the spot.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.460
“You are a--

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.399
Shut up, that meme is outdated!

00:07:42.399 --> 00:07:46.560
The X marks the spot of a photograph proving
that Daniel is the son of Eric and each of

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:50.539
these criminals clearly remembers Eric Matthews
as the man who framed them and got them locked

00:07:50.539 --> 00:07:54.050
up, so they aren’t too happy with the whole
Matthews family in general.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:57.319
To be fair though, they still all did commit
crimes, they just weren’t the same crimes

00:07:57.319 --> 00:07:58.749
that each of them was imprisoned for.

00:07:58.749 --> 00:08:02.399
And to be honest, it’s not like the teenager
Daniel really has any control over the actions

00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:03.399
of his father.

00:08:03.399 --> 00:08:04.659
So maybe they don’t have to be upset with
--

00:08:04.659 --> 00:08:06.520
"OPEN THE ****ING DOOR!!"

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.139
Nope, they’re still mad.

00:08:08.139 --> 00:08:11.870
Laura didn’t last long after that. Xavier
goes off on his own and begins hunting down

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:14.309
the others, so Amanda takes Daniel under her
wing.

00:08:14.309 --> 00:08:18.639
They barricade themselves back in the original
room and discover a trap door under the safe.

00:08:18.639 --> 00:08:21.819
Big brain Daniel is the one to to remember
that when Amanda originally found the tape

00:08:21.819 --> 00:08:25.949
recorder, there was a key alongside it, and
that key is good to unlock the trap door and

00:08:25.949 --> 00:08:27.569
gain access to the basement.

00:08:27.569 --> 00:08:31.020
At this point Xavier has picked off all the
others, and he chases after them in an effort

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:34.020
to collect the numbers shaved into the back
of each of their heads.

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.890
Remember the clue: the numbers are in the
back of your mind.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:40.099
Eventually they make it to the bathroom, where
Daniel does what Adam did in that very same

00:08:40.099 --> 00:08:44.830
room one year earlier and plays dead, in order
to gain the upper hand with a surprise attack

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:45.830
on Xavier.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.830
So yeah.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.340
Daniel kills a man at age 14 or however old
he is.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.280
Let’s give it up for Daniel for being a
bad***.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:54.910
Don’t even type “F” in the comments
for Xavier, let’s just get a big fat BRUH

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:56.330
in the chat for Daniel.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.330
What a little trooper.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.650
With that, the game is over.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:01.730
Daniel’s health is dangerously low, so Amanda
gives him the heart container…

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:05.170
I mean a dose of the antidote to get him through
until the doors open.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:08.601
We don’t actually see this happen, but I’m
assuming that’s what goes down, because

00:09:08.601 --> 00:09:10.290
the needle can be found later on.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:14.170
Amanda helps Daniel get to safety by transporting
him to Jigsaw’s workshop at the Wilson Steel

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.940
Plant, where he’s given an oxygen mask and
stowed away in a safe.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:20.660
I’m guessing the oxygen mask was both to
help him clear the nerve gas from his system

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:24.610
and to keep him breathing in the tiny airspace
of the safe, where he would stay until the

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:25.610
following day.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:29.220
Later that afternoon, Eric is feeling apologetic
about the argument he had with his son, and

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.910
tries to ahold of him, but is obviously unsuccessful.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:35.500
His former partner and mistress Alison Kerry
calls him in to the case of a murder, and

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:39.360
the victim is a man named Michael Marks, an
informant that Matthews has used in the past.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:42.430
Upon arriving at the crime scene, Matthews
is dismissive.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:45.570
Even though this is someone that he knows,
he doesn’t seem to care a whole lot.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:47.890
I think this is because his head isn’t in
the moment.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.750
He’s thinking about his relationship with
his son.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.070
He’s distracted by the pressure of his wife’s
lawyers.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.790
And being around Kerry probably reminds him
of his biggest mistake.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:57.240
(Or at least what he thinks is his biggest
mistake at that point.)

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.510
It’s not until Kerry points it out that
he notices that Jigsaw has left him a little

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:01.000
message.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:01.500
Roll it.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.860
"Look closer Detective Matthews."

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.260
"At what?"

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.360
"Ask whoever wrote it."

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.640
Kerry spends the rest of that day trying to
bring him onto the Jigsaw case, but Eric can’t

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.140
be bothered with it, telling her about all
the other stresses he’s dealing with.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.780
Still, the images of the crime scene stuck
in his head that night until he eventually

00:10:27.782 --> 00:10:28.820
has an epiphany.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:33.060
The steel used in the trap reminded him of
a case from his past at the Wilson Steel Plant.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:36.740
The next day he finally gets out of the office
and turns up in person for the SWAT raid at

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:37.740
Wilson Steel.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.130
Thinking he has gotten the upper hand against
Jigsaw he leans in close, and asks,

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:42.440
“Is this close enough?”

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:46.390
This line demonstrates Mathews’ obsession
with power, which is one of the reasons that

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.820
he’s in the mess he’s in in the first
place.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:52.240
He can’t just catch Jigsaw, he has to gloat
over him, but little does he know, the battle

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:53.720
has only just begun.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:57.780
Unlike the previous criminals he was able
to frame, arrest, and drop easy convictions

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:00.880
on, Eric Matthews had finally met his match
with Jigsaw.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:12.660
Matthews’s men are about to take John Kramer
away, but John tells him he’ll need to remain

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:16.760
in place while Eric deals with a problem in
the other room, a series of monitors showing

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.250
the events of the game in the Nerve Gas House.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:22.360
Eric doesn’t recognise the other criminals
that he'd put away over the years, but he

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.480
does recognize his son, so he confronts Jigsaw
in a rage.

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:29.860
John simply asks Eric for some of his time
for a one on one talk, and promises if he

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.190
can do that he’ll get his son back.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:34.210
“You’ll find your son in a safe and secure
state.”

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.400
Is that a little pun from Jigsaw?

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.870
Because Daniel's in a safe; literally, in
a safe?

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:40.760
His first instinct is to attack Jigsaw.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.630
Again, this tells us a lot about Matthews,
even without seeing much of his past in the

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:45.630
canon.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:49.270
Psychologists often use a person’s first
reaction to make an analysis about them, that’s

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.090
why those Rorschach tests are helpful to make
a diagnosis.

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:55.850
Showing Eric Matthews his son in danger is
essentially Jigsaw’s Rorschach test.

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:59.510
When Eric threatens violence, John reminds
him that he’s already got cancer, so hand

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.170
to hand violence seems pretty insignificant
to him.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:04.670
Jigsaw’s game is simply to test Eric’s
restraint.

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:08.040
If he could sit there and talk to the man
that was responsible for his son’s kidnapping,

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.040
he would pass.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.200
But if he resorted to dirty tactics, like
he did to arrest the other criminals who had

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.810
been in the Nerve Gas House and the other
victims of his police brutality, he would

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:16.850
be punished.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:20.170
Matthews is quickly losing his patience though,
so Kerry tries to get him to take a logical

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:24.190
approach by threatening to destroy the blueprints
of Jigsaw’s traps, but when Matthews puts

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:28.110
this into practice he takes the big, angry,
create a spectacle approach, which is no match

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.820
for John’s cool, casual, intelligent tactics.

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:34.290
“How will you get your conviction without
all of this evidence, Eric?”

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:38.320
The difference in Matthews approach and what
Kerry had in mind is symbolic of the difference

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.660
between a good cop and a dirty cop, as well
as the difference between someone who has

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:45.480
studied Jigsaw and understands him versus
someone who has actively avoided what would

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.680
become the biggest case the city has ever
seen.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:51.620
John’s intention is to tactfully point this
out and make Eric realize the error of his

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:55.250
ways, so as a clue, he tells him to look inside
of a drawer in the other room, which contains

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.130
the arrest files of everyone in the game.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.610
Unfortunately for Eric, he still doesn’t
get the point, and when he notices Xavier

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:05.040
going after Daniel and Amanda on the monitors,
he loses control, and goes full Bashurverse

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:05.920
on the Meltdown Meter.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.980
“You ****ing win okay!?

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:09.400
I'll ****ing go!

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.260
I’LL GOOOO!!!”

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:14.740
He goes into the room with John alone, beats
him up and breaks his finger.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:18.170
He breaks the walkie-talkie in what I see
as an attempt to communicate to John that

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:22.070
he no longer wishes to play by the rules,
if brutality is what it takes, Eric is more

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.200
than willing to go there.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:26.090
When he sticks his gun in John’s mouth,
John has seen enough.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.740
“Game over.”

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.100
He offers to take him to the house where the
game was held.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:33.960
If Eric had just held on and done things by
the book for a little bit longer he would

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:37.870
see that the game on the screens is already
over and his son is tucked away safely.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:41.480
When they arrive at the house, John gives
Eric a key, which he uses to storm in and

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:43.230
find the photo of him and his son.

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:47.210
He ends up searching until he finds himself
underground in the dilapidated bathroom, polluted

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:51.980
by the bodies those tested and failed before
him, and clouded by Eric’s dark desperation

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:52.980
to locate his son.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:56.779
I would guess that clouding is the reason
he momentarily lets his guard down when he

00:13:56.779 --> 00:14:01.190
sees a pale hand at the edge of the bathtub,
perhaps thinking that Daniel was incapacitated

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.691
under the robes and pig mask.

00:14:02.691 --> 00:14:06.410
In reality, it was Amanda, who injects him
with a powerful narcotic before he got the

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:07.450
chance to retaliate.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:11.580
He next wakes up unarmed, with a chain around
his ankle tethering him to the pipe against

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:12.080
the wall.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:15.480
The exact position Adam Stanheight had been
left in one year earlier.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:19.260
Beside him he finds a tape, but unlike the
tapes he neglected to study during the previous

00:14:19.279 --> 00:14:23.960
investigations of Jigsaw murders, this one
emanates the voice of Amanda Young, who condemns

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:27.310
him for framing her on a drug charge for which
she was not guilty.

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:31.150
Amanda has become a disciple of Jigsaw, and
Eric was her first test subject.

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:34.931
The final words of her tape say, “now you
are locked away, helpless and alone,” and

00:14:34.931 --> 00:14:38.500
I find this to be an excellent example of
the punishment fitting the crime.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:42.600
After putting so many guilty people behind
bars the easy way by fudging the evidence,

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:46.870
Eric would now be the one who is locked up
at the mercy of one of the people he has wronged.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:50.720
As this is going on, time expires on Eric’s
game and the safe back at the steel plant

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.020
pops open, setting Daniel free after having
passed his test.

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:55.020
“Game over.”

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:58.840
With Jigsaw’s games, there is always a chance
for redemption, Amanda’s first game would

00:14:58.840 --> 00:14:59.840
be no different.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.470
He finds a flashlight and the hacksaw.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.460
Looking around the room tells him what his
options are.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.770
He sees the bodies of Xavier and Adam, and
the foot of Dr. Gordon.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:10.540
He could choose to take the easy route and
spend the rest of his days in the bathroom,

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:14.090
or suffer through the pain of the trap and
hurt himself to escape.

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:15.540
Mathews gets the gun but it’s not loaded.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:18.840
He’s unable to bring himself to cut his
foot off, but he finds the toilet lid and

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:21.930
uses it to crush the bone in his foot so he
can slide it out of the shackle.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:25.610
I mean, I guess he did this because it’s
faster, but it doesn’t really seem less

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:26.710
painful at all.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.240
It seems like it might be more painful.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.970
Let me know in the comments what you would
prefer though.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:33.610
He’s able to do what my cousin was unable
to after a hefty Thanksgiving dinner, and

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.240
make his way out of the bathroom.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:39.690
But like my cousin, his suffering for that
evening did not end there, because Eric Matthews

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:42.640
would encounter an enemy on the other side
of that door.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:53.840
Detective Matthews, after finding a pipe that
he uses as a crutch, continues to search for

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:58.250
his son Daniel, but what he finds instead
is his captor, Amanda and the two engage in

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.839
a physical altercation.

00:15:59.839 --> 00:16:02.950
Matthews finds himself in position to take
her out before his broken foot becomes an

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:03.950
issue.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:06.110
And then… he bites Amanda’s leg for some
reason.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.110
“AHHHHH!”

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:08.370
"This is delicious!"

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:12.600
He gets a hold of Amanda and it seems his
old ways have not changed, because he tries

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.760
to beat the location of Daniel out of her.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:18.220
She refuses to cooperate, and he’s about
to finish her off when she goes for his weak

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:19.800
foot and scrambles away.

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:24.020
Amanda is going to leave him like that, but
even in excruciating pain, Matthews true nature

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:27.510
shines through, and once again he can’t
just leave things be.

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:31.250
“You’re not Jigsaw *****. You hear me?

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:32.500
You’re nothing!”

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:36.160
Amanda comes back and we don’t see exactly
what happens after that, but Jigsaw would

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:39.680
later describe her actions as ‘leaving him
for dead’, so I’d say she mostly likely

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.830
attempted to kill him.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.630
She even believes he's dead after those events,
but he’s actually able to survive somehow,

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:48.190
partially thanks to John Kramer going back
into the house and, as he puts it, cleaning

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.620
up Amanda’s mistake.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:53.380
What happens next is not really in line with
the usual treatment of those who survive one

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:54.680
of Jigsaw’s games though.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:58.170
Rather than immediately attempting to convert
Matthews into one of his followers, I think

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:00.930
John realizes that Amanda’s test did not
work on Matthews.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:05.149
He had not rehabilitated like the other survivors
had, because he still tried to use force to

00:17:05.149 --> 00:17:07.410
obtain the location of his son after escaping.

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:10.860
He's put into a cell down the hall in order
to reflect on his crimes, where he is given

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.669
an orange jumpsuit to bring him down to the
level of those he imprisoned.

00:17:13.669 --> 00:17:17.720
He’s also given a foot brace and he’s
periodically fed some kind of goop through

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:18.829
a small slot.

00:17:18.829 --> 00:17:20.949
Matthews is deliberately kept alive for the
next six months.

00:17:20.949 --> 00:17:22.660
And he makes a furry little friend.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:29.780
His confinement would end on April 28th, 2006,
when he’s taken to the Gideon Meat Packing

00:17:29.789 --> 00:17:32.769
Plant for another game; another chance at
redemption.

00:17:32.769 --> 00:17:36.970
He’s forced to barefoot on a large block
of ice with a noose around his neck as a timer

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:39.179
in the room counts down from 90 minutes.

00:17:39.179 --> 00:17:42.899
As he takes in more of his surroundings, he
realizes that his fellow officer, Detective

00:17:42.899 --> 00:17:45.390
Mark Hoffman is strapped down to a chair beside
him.

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:48.670
Another man walks into the room and pulls
a chain, which activates a contraption on

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.280
the ceiling above Matthews.

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:53.429
Eventually, after all he had been through,
he can’t take it anymore, and steps off

00:17:53.429 --> 00:17:56.659
the ice block to try to off himself and end
his own suffering.

00:17:56.659 --> 00:18:00.429
This gets the captor’s attention and he
picks Eric back up onto the ice block, explaining

00:18:00.429 --> 00:18:03.629
that if he doesn’t weigh down the block,
the water melted off of the ice will run down

00:18:03.629 --> 00:18:06.610
hill and electrocute his friend Detective
Hoffman.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:10.769
Eric reluctantly decides to stay put, not
wanting to sacrifice the life of another just

00:18:10.769 --> 00:18:12.370
so he can take the easy way out.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:14.980
This part highlights the dynamic aspect of
Matthews character.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:18.889
In his first game he’s made out to be selfish
and lazy, but he clearly does care about his

00:18:18.889 --> 00:18:21.649
son, and I think the same can be said about
his comrade Hoffman.

00:18:21.649 --> 00:18:25.230
With just under 20 minutes left on the timer,
Matthews pretends to lose consciousness, once

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:28.700
again drawing the attention of the captor,
but this time when he uses the close proximity

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:29.700
to attack him.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:33.420
He holds his feet down, again, saving Hoffman
from electrocution, and tells Matthews, “I’m

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.309
not the one you gotta worry about, you understand
me?”

00:18:35.309 --> 00:18:39.110
He divulges a little more information, telling
Matthews and Hoffman that there’s another

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:42.740
guy being tested, and if he passes, all of
them get to go free.

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:46.369
By making Eric stand on the ice block for
90 minutes, Jigsaw is testing his will to

00:18:46.369 --> 00:18:48.649
live after being locked up for 6 months.

00:18:48.649 --> 00:18:51.619
With the next phase of the game, he’s going
to test if Matthews learned anything in their

00:18:51.619 --> 00:18:55.690
previous game -- if he’s learned to restrain
himself and let justice play out as Jigsaw

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:59.779
intends it to, or if he’s going to interfere
and take punishments into his own hands like

00:18:59.779 --> 00:19:03.860
he did with the seven criminals and with Jigsaw
himself back at the Wilson Steel Plant.

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:07.750
To do this, Jigsaw has instructed the captor
to hand Eric a gun and a bullet.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:11.519
With 19 minutes and six seconds remaining,
he gives Matthews the power to make his own

00:19:11.519 --> 00:19:13.230
choice on what he wants to do with it.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:17.070
When the timer gets below one minute, their
captor takes out a red button, which is supposed

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:20.659
to release them from their traps after the
time expires, as long as the fourth guy doesn’t

00:19:20.659 --> 00:19:21.700
come through the door.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:25.419
Matthews spots the other guy running up beyond
the translucent glass and tries to yell out

00:19:25.419 --> 00:19:30.320
to warn him not to open it, but with just
two seconds left, the man, SWAT Officer Rigg

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:34.100
(who is another one of their fellow law enforcement
guys) charges the door to break it down.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:37.640
As a last ditch effort, Matthews shoots the
glass, but this would not be enough to save

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:38.640
him.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:42.159
Upon the opening of the door the contraption
him is released, and two huge ice blocks swing

00:19:42.159 --> 00:19:46.669
down and crush his head, putting an end to
his long six months of suffering.

00:19:46.669 --> 00:19:50.120
In the end, it seems that Eric Matthews story
is kind of a tragic one.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:53.570
In the beginning he’s stubborn and does
things his way, but ultimately pays the price

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:57.990
for it, having to break his own foot and suffer
six months of solitary confinement to survive,

00:19:57.990 --> 00:20:01.940
only to make it to a test where he suffered
even more, only to find out his life was in

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:04.020
the hands of Officer Rigg the whole time.

00:20:04.029 --> 00:20:07.580
I think the argument can be made that by the
time Rigg came through that door, Matthews

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.669
actually had rehabilitated in a way.

00:20:09.669 --> 00:20:13.639
He shows an act of selflessness by suffering
to keep Hoffman alive even when he no longer

00:20:13.639 --> 00:20:17.230
wanted to go on, and he did manage to play
by the rules during his second game.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:21.610
One thing I find interesting is that Jigsaw’s
victims usually do have some chance to redeem

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.999
themselves, but Matthews life seemed to be
entirely in the hands of Rigg.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:28.850
The event of Rigg coming through the door
and Matthews firing the gun all happens at

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:33.540
once, so I’m wondering if maybe it’s possible
that Matthews was actually given a second chance.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:37.250
Maybe there are actually two requirements
that must be met in order for the ice blocks

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.340
above his head to be released.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.659
The first is obviously for Rigg to come through
the door before time expires.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:45.820
As for the second, let’s say that there's a
microphone in the room somewhere use to detect

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:51.300
any loud noises above 140dB, so if Matthews
end up firing the gun, the device detects

00:20:51.309 --> 00:20:53.960
that as the second requirement to release
the ice blocks.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:57.169
Of course, this isn’t shown anywhere in
the movie, this is just an idea that I had,

00:20:57.169 --> 00:20:59.970
but I think it falls more in line with Jigsaw’s
values.

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:04.650
So that ends the story of Eric Matthews, but
perhaps the Matthews name lives on… because

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:08.410
as far as we know, Matthews son Daniel is
still alive.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:12.809
As we know, survivors of Jigsaw’s game often
become his followers, his disciples, the ones

00:21:12.809 --> 00:21:14.600
to carry out his legacy.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:19.280
Perhaps we will see Daniel Matthews again
in a future Saw movie… or perhaps we already

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:19.780
have.

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:23.139
At the end of Saw 7, spoiler alert if you
haven’t watched that far for some reason...

00:21:23.139 --> 00:21:26.330
(And yes, I’m aware it’s called Saw 3D:
The Final Chapter or whatever; I prefer to

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:30.350
call it Saw 7) But yeah, at the end of Saw
7 we learn that Dr. Lawrence Gordon has been

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:34.539
helping Jigsaw behind the scenes all along,
and he captures Hoffman with the aid of two

00:21:34.539 --> 00:21:35.539
masked henchman.

00:21:35.539 --> 00:21:39.279
I know in the deleted scenes it turns out
to be these two cucks, but there’s a reason

00:21:39.279 --> 00:21:43.960
that scenes are deleted, and intended storylines
do change as the Saw series plays out sometimes.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:47.980
As far as I’m concerned, the identity of
these two is up in the air as far as the canon

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.600
goes for future installments.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:53.580
In the past I’ve theorized that one of them
could be Logan Nelson, but I think another

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:58.470
possibility for the true identity of one of
these henchman could be… none other than…

00:21:58.470 --> 00:22:00.840
Bradley Donovan -- I’ll see you all tomorrow
night!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.940
Assuming we both survive!

